<h2>Executive Summary</h2>
<table class="stats">
  <tr>
    <td><span class="stat-num n-total">33</span><span class="stat-lbl">Total Fixes</span></td>
    <td><span class="stat-num n-p0">5</span><span class="stat-lbl">P0 Critical</span></td>
    <td><span class="stat-num n-p1">12</span><span class="stat-lbl">P1 High</span></td>
    <td><span class="stat-num n-p2">12</span><span class="stat-lbl">P2 Medium</span></td>
    <td><span class="stat-num n-p3">4</span><span class="stat-lbl">P3 Low</span></td>
    <td><span class="stat-num n-accent">2</span><span class="stat-lbl">New Pages</span></td>
    <td><span class="stat-num n-accent">20</span><span class="stat-lbl">Files Changed</span></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p>
  Two sequential deep-scan audit passes were performed across the entire codebase —
  frontend React application, backend Express API, Mongoose data models, seeding utilities,
  and deployment configuration. Issues were categorised by impact severity from P0
  (runtime crash or data corruption) down to P3 (minor polish). All 33 identified
  defects were resolved and the final production build passes with zero errors.
</p>

<h3>Severity Scale</h3>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:12%">Level</th>
    <th>Definition</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p0">P0</span></td><td>Runtime crash, data corruption, or silent auth bypass — blocks a core user journey</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td><td>Wrong behaviour, broken flow, or logic error with a clear negative user impact</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td><td>Incorrect data, misleading copy, invalid CSS, or redundant computation</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p3">P3</span></td><td>Minor UX gap, missing guard, or low-risk omission</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

