<div class="pagebreak"></div>
<div class="phase-div">&#9644;&nbsp; Phase 1 — Deployment &amp; Core Fixes &nbsp;&#9644;</div>

<!-- 1. Auth & Routing -->
<h2>1. Authentication &amp; Routing</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Description of Fix</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/Orders.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p0">P0 · Crash</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Orders never loaded.</strong> API response was unwrapped as <code>data.data</code> but the endpoint returns <code>data.orders</code>. Fixed to <code>data.orders || data.data || []</code> with array guard.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/components/Breadcrumb.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Navigation links silently failed.</strong> Some pages passed a <code>url</code> prop, others a <code>to</code> prop. Component only read <code>url</code>. Fixed to resolve <code>item.url || item.to</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/TrackOrder.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Track Order showed stale results.</strong> <code>useEffect</code> had empty <code>[]</code> deps (ignored URL param changes), <code>province</code> field name mismatched DB field <code>state</code>, and state was not reset before re-fetch. All three corrected.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 2. UX & Dialogs -->
<h2>2. UX &amp; Native Dialogs</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Description of Fix</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/OrderDetails.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Cancel order used <code>window.confirm</code> and <code>alert()</code></strong> — both block the main thread and break the custom UI. Replaced with an inline confirm/cancel button pattern and <code>showToast()</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/components/Footer.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Four invalid Tailwind classes</strong> (<code>bg-stone-805</code>, <code>border-stone-850</code>, <code>text-xxs</code> ×2) rendered without styles. Dead <code>&lt;a href="#privacy"&gt;</code> anchors replaced with router <code>&lt;Link&gt;</code>. Newsletter form rewritten with proper email regex validation and distinct error / already-subscribed / success states.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 3. New Pages -->
<h2>3. New Pages &amp; Features</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Description of Fix</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/ResetPassword.jsx<br><br>src/routes/AppRoutes.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-new">New Page</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Password reset flow was incomplete — the landing page was missing.</strong> Created new page at <code>/reset-password/:token</code> with: password + confirm fields, strength validation (8+ characters, uppercase letter, digit), contextual server error display with a link to re-request the token, and auto-redirect to <code>/login</code> after 4 seconds on success. Route registered as a lazy-loaded public route in AppRoutes.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/Home.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p0">P0 · Crash</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Home crashed when banners array was empty.</strong> Carousel prev/next buttons and dot nav only render when <code>banners.length &gt; 1</code>. A static fallback hero section renders when <code>banners.length === 0</code>.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 4. Deployment -->
<h2>4. Vercel Deployment &amp; Backend Hardening</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Description of Fix</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">frontend/vercel.json</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-new">Created</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>SPA routing config for Vercel.</strong> Rewrites all routes to <code>index.html</code>, declares Vite build command, output directory, and long-term immutable cache headers for hashed asset files.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">backend/vercel.json</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-new">Created</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Serverless Express on Vercel.</strong> Uses <code>@vercel/node</code> builder for <code>server.js</code>, routes all traffic to the Express handler, and injects <code>VERCEL=1</code> environment flag to skip <code>app.listen()</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">backend/server.js</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>CORS rejected Vercel preview deployment URLs; rate limiter saw proxy IP instead of real client IP.</strong> Added <code>app.set("trust proxy", 1)</code>. CORS changed from a single static origin string to a dynamic function that allows: localhost, configured <code>FRONTEND_URL</code>, any <code>*.vercel.app</code> subdomain (preview deployments), and a comma-separated <code>ADDITIONAL_ORIGINS</code> env var. <code>app.listen()</code> is skipped when <code>VERCEL=1</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">backend/.env.example<br>frontend/.env.example</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Both <code>.env.example</code> files updated</strong> with complete variable sets: Cloudinary credentials, optional SMTP email, <code>ADDITIONAL_ORIGINS</code>, and comments explaining production vs. development values.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
     PHASE 2
═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="pagebreak"></div>
<div class="phase-div">&#9644;&nbsp; Phase 2 — Deep Scan &amp; Systematic Repair &nbsp;&#9644;</div>

<!-- 5. P0 Crashes -->
<h2>5. P0 — Runtime Crashes</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Description of Fix</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/components/Rating.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p0">P0</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong><code>value.toFixed(1)</code> threw a TypeError on null / undefined.</strong> Any product without a rating value would crash every page that renders the Rating component in <code>showText</code> mode (product cards, product detail, wishlist). Fixed to <code>(value ?? 0).toFixed(1)</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/context/AuthContext.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p0">P0</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Registration silently left users unauthenticated.</strong> <code>authService.register()</code> stored the JWT in localStorage but the React context (<code>isAuthenticated</code>, <code>user</code>) was never updated — meaning the user appeared logged out immediately after registering. Added <code>authenticate(userData)</code> method that sets both state values synchronously. Also changed <code>login()</code> to return the user object instead of the boolean <code>true</code>, eliminating a downstream race condition in <code>Login.jsx</code>.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 6. P1 Auth & Commerce -->
<h2>6. P1 — Auth Flow &amp; Commerce Logic</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Description of Fix</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/Register.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p0">P0 → Fixed</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col">
        <strong>Three defects resolved:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Registration never called <code>authenticate()</code> — user appeared logged out after sign-up. Now calls <code>authenticate(data.user)</code> on API success.</li>
          <li>Weak email regex <code>/\S+@\S+\.\S+/</code> accepted invalid addresses. Replaced with the same RFC-pattern used in Login.</li>
          <li>Error toast type was <code>"info"</code> — changed to <code>"error"</code> so the toast renders in the correct red/alert style.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/Login.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Post-login role was read from <code>localStorage</code> after <code>await login()</code></strong> — a race condition because React state updates are asynchronous and the stored value was sometimes stale or from a previous session. Now reads the user object returned directly from <code>login()</code>. Auth failure toasts changed from <code>"info"</code> to <code>"error"</code> type.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/components/ProtectedRoute.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Login redirect lost the destination URL.</strong> Unauthenticated users were sent to <code>/login</code> with no way to return to their intended page. Changed to <code>/login?returnTo=&lt;encoded-path&gt;</code> using <code>useLocation</code>. Also fixed the loading spinner: the store-name label had <code>mt-24</code> (absolute bottom offset) which clipped on small screens — changed to <code>top-full mt-2</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/Cart.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Coupon discount scaled incorrectly when cart quantity changed.</strong> The discount was stored as a fraction of the subtotal at the moment of validation (<code>discountValue / subtotal</code>) and then multiplied back at render time. Adding or removing items changed the subtotal, causing the coupon amount to drift. Fixed to store and apply the absolute PKR discount value directly.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/Checkout.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col">
        <strong>Two coupon defects:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Typing any character in the coupon input called <code>setCouponApplied(null)</code> on every keystroke — clearing a previously applied coupon while the user was still typing a new one. Removed from <code>onChange</code>.</li>
          <li>A coupon applied in the Cart page was not carried to Checkout. Added <code>useLocation</code> and a mount effect that reads <code>location.state?.appliedCouponCode</code> and auto-validates it via the API when the Checkout page loads.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/ProductDetails.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>"Buy Now" routed to <code>/cart</code> instead of <code>/checkout</code></strong> — defeating the purpose of the button by dumping the user back at the cart review page rather than proceeding to purchase. Corrected to <code>navigate("/checkout")</code>. Also removed hardcoded fake color variants <code>["Tan", "Black", "Burgundy"]</code> that appeared alongside the real product color — only the product's actual <code>color</code> field is shown.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 7. QuickView Modal -->
<h2>7. P1 — QuickView Modal</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Description of Fix</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/components/QuickViewModal.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p1">P1</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col">
        <strong>Three defects in one component:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Exit animation never played.</strong> <code>if (!product) return null</code> appeared before <code>&lt;AnimatePresence&gt;</code> — returning null before AnimatePresence could track the element meant the closing animation was always skipped. Restructured to wrap <code>{"{"}product &amp;&amp; &lt;div&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;{"}"}</code> inside AnimatePresence.</li>
          <li><strong>Hardcoded color swatches</strong> <code>["Tan", "Black", "Burgundy"]</code> were appended regardless of the actual product — showing non-existent colour options. Replaced with only the real product colour.</li>
          <li><strong>Optional chaining added</strong> to all product field accesses (<code>product?.stock ?? 0</code>) so the modal cannot throw if the parent passes a partially-loaded product object.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 8. P2 Quality -->
<div class="pagebreak"></div>
<h2>8. P2 — Code Quality &amp; Correctness</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Description of Fix</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/context/SettingsContext.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Default currency was "USD" on a PKR-only platform.</strong> Changed <code>currency: "USD"</code> to <code>"PKR"</code>. Updated the announcement bar default from <em>"Free Priority Shipping On Orders Over $150…"</em> to <em>"Free Priority Shipping On Orders Over Rs. 20,000…"</em> — eliminating the incorrect currency symbol shown to users before settings load from the API.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/context/WishlistContext.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong><code>JSON.parse(s)</code> called twice</strong> in the localStorage read helper — the second call wastes CPU and could in theory produce inconsistent results on malformed JSON (e.g. if a getter has side effects). Cached as <code>const parsed = JSON.parse(s)</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/UserProfile.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>AddressForm used <code>alert()</code> for validation feedback</strong> — blocking the main thread and bypassing the app's toast design system. Added <code>useToast()</code> inside the <code>AddressForm</code> sub-component and replaced all three <code>alert()</code> calls with <code>showToast("…", "error")</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/About.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Three invalid Tailwind CSS classes rendered without any styles:</strong> <code>border-amber-450</code> → <code>border-amber-400</code>, <code>text-xxs</code> → <code>text-[10px]</code>, <code>bg-stone-850</code> → <code>bg-stone-900</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/NotFound.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Two invalid classes:</strong> <code>animate-duration-5000</code> (a Tailwind plugin class that is not installed) removed and replaced with an inline <code>style={{ "{{" }}animationDuration: "5s"{{ "}}" }}</code>. Both instances of <code>text-xxs</code> → <code>text-[10px]</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">src/pages/Wishlist.jsx</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Toast copy read "cart list"</strong> when moving an item from the wishlist to the cart — grammatically awkward and inconsistent with the rest of the UI. Changed to <em>"Moved … to your cart."</em></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 9. Backend -->
<h2>9. Backend — Models, Routes &amp; Seed</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Description of Fix</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">backend/models/User.js<br>backend/models/Order.js</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Default country was <code>"US"</code></strong> on both the address sub-schema in the User model and the shipping address schema in the Order model. Changed to <code>"Pakistan"</code> — consistent with the checkout form default and the platform's target market.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">backend/utils/seed.js</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p2">P2</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col">
        <strong>Two defects:</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Seed address fixtures used key <code>province</code> but the Order model schema defines the field as <code>state</code> — causing all seeded orders to have a blank province. All four address helper functions updated.</li>
          <li><code>dropDatabase()</code> had no environment guard — could wipe a production database if the script were accidentally run against a live MongoDB URI. Added <code>if (NODE_ENV === "production") process.exit(1)</code> before the drop call.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="file-col">backend/routes/authRoutes.js</td>
      <td class="sev-col"><span class="badge b-p3">P3</span></td>
      <td class="desc-col"><strong>Logout route had no authentication middleware.</strong> Any unauthenticated request could invoke the logout controller unnecessarily. Added the <code>protect</code> middleware: <code>router.post("/logout", protect, logout)</code>.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- 10. Shop -->
<h2>10. P3 — Shop Page Polish</h2>
<table class="fixes">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:28%">File</th>
